RULES
- No hard-coded dimensions outside params.py. Use named variables.
- Don't invent standards, material properties or part numbers; mark unknowns TODO.
- Flag uncertainty instead of guessing; list open questions in README.md.
- Keep functions small with docstrings so a student can explain each line to an instructor.
- After each step, stop and wait for review.
- Do not claim the design is validated. Only prototype tests can do that.
- Keep code simple and readable. Ask before adding any library beyond CadQuery, cq_gears, numpy.
